# Judgment-aware use of Agent Skills (optional, project-level guidance)

Apply relevant Skills for their domain knowledge, tools, and mandatory requirements. Treat optional examples and defaults as task-dependent rather than universal. When flexibility is explicitly permitted and would improve the outcome, use task-sensitive judgment instead of mechanically combining templates. Do not weaken higher-priority rules, user requirements, security checks, format/tool contracts, or genuinely required Skill procedures. Do not add brainstorming or alternative-generation overhead to deterministic tasks. Evaluate completed work for both compliance and suitability; do not claim benefits without evidence.

This snippet is guidance in its installation context, not a new higher-priority authority layer. Where other instructions have higher priority, follow them.
